{#
    Anonymous component: <twig:SurvosFw:Ks:QrCode data="https://example.com" />

    A QR code linking to `data`, wrapped in an <a> so it's clickable too (not just
    scannable) -- the "scan to open this on your phone" pattern used on pgsc's
    landing.html.twig, rutado's home/index.html.twig, and dadjokes' home/index.html.twig,
    now extracted here instead of hand-copied a fourth time. Self-hosted: qr_code_url()
    (endroid/qr-code-bundle, a hard dependency of this bundle) renders the PNG via a real
    route on your own server, no third-party API call, no data ever leaves your app.
#}
{% props data, size = 150, caption = 'Scan to open on your phone', alt = null, target = '_blank' %}
<figure class="text-center">
    {# target defaults to _blank: on desktop this is a "scan to open on your
       phone" QR code, but it's also just a link -- clicking it shouldn't
       navigate away from the page you're looking at (e.g. a marketing
       homepage), and it's what lets you click-to-test the target app in a
       second local tab instead of a real phone. #}
    <a href="{{ data }}"{% if target %} target="{{ target }}" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>
        <img src="{{ qr_code_url(data) }}" alt="{{ alt ?? caption }}" style="max-width: {{ size }}px">
    </a>
    {% if caption %}
        <figcaption class="text-secondary small mt-1">{{ caption }}</figcaption>
    {% endif %}
</figure>
